WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:00.800
The woman

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.568
once considered

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.636
Australia's worst female serial killer,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.339
is enjoying her first taste of freedom

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.074
since 2003.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:08.942
Kathleen Folbigg,

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:09.776
who was pardoned

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.910
Monday over the death

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.178
of four of her babies

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.181
earlier released this video statement.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.883
My eternal gratitude

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.052
goes to my friends and family,

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.554
especially Tracy and all of her family,

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:22.989
and I would not have survived

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.624
this whole ordeal without them.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.526
Today is a victory for science

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.061
and especially truth.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.529
And for the last 20 years,

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.031
I have been in prison.

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:33.466
I have forever and will always

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.601
think of my children,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.802
great for my children.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.937
And I miss them and love them terribly.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:38.838
Thank you.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.908
On her first day out of prison

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:42.776
in 20 years,

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:44.544
according to her childhood friend MS.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.246
Folbigg had a cup of tea

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.281
and enjoyed a good night's sleep.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.549
She was convicted of killing her

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.250
young children

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.386
over a decade from 1989 to 1999.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.255
But new evidence found

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.656
a genetic defect caused

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.458
at least three of the deaths.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:00:59.659
Those children.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.260
Joining us now

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.528
from the Australian capital,

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:02.295
Canberra, Anna-Maria

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.563
Arabia is the CEO

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.465
of the Australian Academy of Sciences.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.032
One of the parties

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.767
that actually managed to get this case

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.402
managed to get this part in for her.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.204
So thank you so much for being with us.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.305
We really appreciate your time.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:14.274
I just want to

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.075
help with the

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.676
thought here, which seems unshakable.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.710
Is that MS.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.378
Folbigg spent

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.146
not only two decades in prison

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.515
for a crime he didn't commit.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:23.083
At the same time,

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.251
she was accused of killing her children,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.186
but also dealing

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:27.954
with the grief of their death.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.623
It just seems two decades of hell.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:35.161
It's unimaginable trauma and grief.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:38.965
And in all of our scientific work

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.767
to support this case,

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.803
it has been difficult to imagine

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:46.139
what she has been through.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:49.175
But we have kept in our minds

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.678
the thought that behind this case

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:54.047
and all of the scientific evidence,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:57.417
there is a woman who has experienced

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:01.521
immense trauma and grief in her life.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.022
It really is unimaginable

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.891
for us, I believe.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.826
Explain to me the science of how

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:08.495
this all began.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:08.828
You've actually

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:09.329
had her name

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:09.696
cleared, how

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:10.630
this pardon came about,

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.065
what your role in all this

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.099
and how you came into this

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.601
in the first place.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.135
Yes.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.504
She was convicted in 2003.

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.505
And of course, at that time,

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:19.305
the human genome

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.473
was just being sequenced.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.674
And none of the information

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.676
that has led to her

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.879
pardon was available at the time.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.213
There was a first inquiry

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.481
into the convictions of Kathleen

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.851
Folbigg held in 2019, and at that time

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.688
there were the genome of both Kathleen

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.857
and her four children was sequenced

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.159
and the analysis around

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:41.327
that genomic sequence had had commenced.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.663
And indeed in 2019

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.999
some mutations are rare,

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.168
genetic mutations were found to be held

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.002
by both Katherine

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:49.969
Kathleen

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.338
and her children and her two daughters

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.841
and it was on the strength

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.742
of that evidence

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:56.142
and each

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.344
being presented in a preliminary sense

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.979
at that first inquiry

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.549
and really not being adequately explored

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.551
that one of our fellows

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.152
of the Australian Academy of Science

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.021
Professor Carolyn Weiser,

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.055
approached us

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:09.556
and said

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.524
We do need to look at this further.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:11.991
You know,

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.293
there is more information

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.060
available here

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.129
in the Australian justice system

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:19.132
Does need to hear

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.333
full and comprehensive

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.702
scientific evidence around this case.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.772
And so began our investigation

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.440
of the science and Professor Van

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.342
Weiss's efforts to

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.843
reach out to experts

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.779
right around the world

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.180
to ask for their help,

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.649
their specific expertize

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.850
to help understand

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.019
what this genetic mutation meant.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.355
And over time

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.823
it's become very clear

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.791
that the cow module

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.160
and mutation held by Kathleen

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.729
and her daughters is rare

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:53.466
and is a likely cause of death via

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:54.901
cardiac arrhythmia.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.135
So a sudden

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.503
stopping of the heart

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.472
that can lead to death

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.140
and in this case is likely

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.610
to have occurred for her two daughters.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.912
There was also an enormous

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.746
body of evidence

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.714
around the health

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.315
or should I say ill health

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.717
of her two sons.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:12.452
One of her

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:15.088
sons, Patrick, had epilepsy

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.925
and indeed died after a seizure

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.827
and had suffered some

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.862
ill health over his life.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:23.930
And Caleb died,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.965
unfortunately, at 19 days,

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.767
and he was unable to swallow

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.235
and breathe at the same time.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.471
He had a respiratory illness,

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.172
which was quite acute

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.574
and then led to his death.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.175
So this

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.711
collective body of scientific evidence,

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:39.679
as well

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.047
as scientific evidence

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.549
to analyze diaries and journals

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.550
that Kathleen Folbigg

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.418
had kept

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:48.154
all came together in this second inquiry

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.922
that has led the commission

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:50.657
of the inquiry,

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:51.291
the Honorable

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.892
Tom Bathurst, to arrive

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.694
at a very firm conclusion

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.396
that there are natural causes of death

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.331
for all of the Folbigg children

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.066
and that he strongly recommended

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:01.868
that she be pardoned

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.069
or that there'd be reasonable

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.570
doubt as to her convictions

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.606
which then led the Attorney-General

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:08.875
of New South Wales to recommend a pardon

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.143
which has been granted

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.578
leading to her release yesterday.

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.347
Yeah, it's an incredible story

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.683
the science is amazing.

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:18.718
Just it took so long obviously, but

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.320
this is how these things are

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.387
and 20 years in jail

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.089
just seems like a very long time.

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.525
But it seems that justice has been done,

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:25.925
I guess,

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.627
and that she is now a free woman

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.162
and he's staying with us.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.564
And congratulations on all your work.

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:33.800
It's a great outcome.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.501
Thanks so much. Thank you.

